# @NAME@ — ESPboy

Build: `pio run`. Serial upload of **both matching images**: `pio run -t upload`.

| Flash offset | Contents | Limit |
|---|---|---|
| `0x00000` | `.pio/build/espboy/firmware.bin` (includes eboot) | 256 KiB |
| `0x40000` | `rom.bin`, raw or partially LZSS packed | 748 KiB |
| `0xFB000` | Reserved calibration/configuration sectors | 20 KiB |

ESP8266/LX106, 1 MiB flash, 128×128 ST7735. Runs at 160 MHz; the shared menu
also offers 80 MHz. No SD, filesystem or networking. The linker bounds the
application region; a post-build check also bounds the actual upload binary.
The cartridge occupies its own mapped flash area, leaving the entire program
budget available to the runtime and compiled code.

Game Boy DMG cartridges only for this first ESPboy version. The recompiler,
interpreter, mapper, PPU, APU, palettes, input/menu and vertical scaling are
shared with META/Pokitto. Horizontal output reduces 160 to 128 without
cropping; frames are sent as strips without a framebuffer. ROM byte reads
use aligned flash loads on Xtensa. Native ARM assembly and `--meta-thumb`
are unavailable; the firmware compiler is GCC.

Storage is raw whenever it fits. Otherwise the shared 512-byte LZSS codec
compresses only enough sectors to fit (largest byte savings first), keeping
bank 0 raw; the existing runtime sector cache decodes them on demand. There
is no SD fallback: an incompressible cartridge which exceeds the physical
flash is rejected during generation. `--meta-pack` is accepted but never
forces compression when raw already fits. `--meta-stream on` is rejected.

The startup uses the Arduino 3.1.2 image tooling and peripheral drivers but
runs a single task directly, without the non-OS SDK/network startup. ROM
interrupt services drive timer1 audio; the cycle counter supplies time at
both CPU speeds. The program uses the boot stack, separately from cartridge
RAM. Cartridge RAM works in RAM; battery saves and save states do not persist.

ACT = A, ESC = B, right auxiliary = Start, left auxiliary tap = Select;
hold left auxiliary for the shared menu. Quit resets the ESP8266.

Wiring: HSPI MOSI GPIO13 / SCK GPIO14, LCD DC GPIO15, MCP23017 at `0x20`
(buttons PA0..7, LCD CS PB0), I²C SDA GPIO4 / SCL GPIO5, MCP4725 backlight
at `0x60`, speaker GPIO0. Panel offsets: (2, 3), MADCTL `0xC8`.

References:
- https://github.com/ESPboy-edu/ESPboy_FirstTest
- https://github.com/m1cr0lab-espboy/ESPboy/blob/main/src/ESPboy.cpp
- https://github.com/m1cr0lab-espboy/ESPboy/blob/main/src/ESPboy.h
- https://github.com/esp8266/Arduino/tree/3.1.2/bootloaders/eboot

Validation is host differential testing and Xtensa compilation/size checks.
Startup, panel, input and sound still need verification on an actual ESPboy.
